	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Stonetalon Mountains are a wall of grey peaks and deep green valleys in the west of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, between the forests of {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link} to the north and the plains of {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link} and {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link} to the south and east. At their crown stands {link:stonetalon-peak}Stonetalon Peak{/link}, a height long held sacred by the druids of the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link}. Below it the land falls away into lakes, gorges and forests of towering trees. Many of those trees are gone now. The {link:venture-company}Venture Company{/link} has come to Stonetalon with saws and fire, and where its machines have passed, the spirits of the land cry out in pain.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records how the mountains were raised, or who first named them. What is known is that Stonetalon was a holy place long before the younger races came to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. The {link:night-elves}kaldorei{/link} druids built the {link:the-talon-den}Talon Den{/link} high on the peak and kept their treasures within it. Among the stones of the summit lie the ruins of an older work still: a temple from the age of {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link}, whose makers are remembered by few and mourned by fewer. The forest that clothed the valleys below was the charge of the sons and daughters of the demigod {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link}, and it grew undisturbed for longer than any mortal can reckon.

In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, the peak entered the history of the younger races. It was to Stonetalon that {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne Bloodhoof{/link} sent the young warchief {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}, in search of an Oracle who dwelt in the mountain. There the leaders of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} and the humans of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} met the prophet who had summoned them west, and learned that he was {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Stonetalon is a land at war with itself. Goblins of the {link:venture-company}Venture Company{/link} have fallen upon the forests of {link:windshear-crag}Windshear Crag{/link}, and their shredders fell in an hour what grew for a thousand years. When they pushed into the {link:the-charred-vale}Charred Vale{/link}, something in the vale fought back, and the goblins burned it in their retreat. Fire elementals now walk the ashes. The Bloodfury {link:harpies}harpies{/link} have made their nests among the blackened hills, and from there they spread across the whole of the continent.

Neither the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} nor the {link:horde}Horde{/link} will abandon the mountains. The night elves hold {link:stonetalon-peak}Stonetalon Peak{/link}, and a Sentinel and a {link:gnomes}gnome{/link} mage work together against the goblins at the edge of Windshear Crag. The Horde holds {link:sun-rock-retreat}Sun Rock Retreat{/link} in the heart of the range, where {link:tauren}tauren{/link} and orcs seek to heal the land. At {link:malaka-jin}Malaka'jin{/link}, in the far south, trolls of the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} hunt and brew. To the south-east, the {link:grimtotem-clan}Grimtotem{/link} have raised a war camp of their own. All of them agree on one thing: the Venture Company must go. They agree on little else.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:night-elves}kaldorei{/link} of the peak.{/b} Druids and {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} keep {link:stonetalon-peak}Stonetalon Peak{/link} and the {link:the-talon-den}Talon Den{/link}. They are few, and they are watchful.
• {b}The {link:horde}Horde{/link} of {link:sun-rock-retreat}Sun Rock{/link}.{/b} {link:tauren}Tauren{/link}, orcs and those who have come to fight beside them hold Sun Rock Retreat, the only safe roof between the {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link} and {link:desolace}Desolace{/link}.
• {b}The {link:venture-company}Venture Company{/link}.{/b} Goblin loggers, miners and engineers work {link:windshear-crag}Windshear Crag{/link} with great machines, guarded by hired hands.
• {b}The Bloodfury harpies.{/b} They nest in the {link:the-charred-vale}Charred Vale{/link}, and their queen rules them from its western hills.
• {b}The Grimtotem.{/b} A war band of this tauren clan holds {link:grimtotem-post}Grimtotem Post{/link} in the south-east and raids the villages of its own people.
• {b}Kobolds, spiders and wyverns.{/b} {link:kobolds}Kobolds{/link} mine the depths of {link:boulderslide-ravine}Boulderslide Ravine{/link}. Great spiders hunt the {link:webwinder-path}Webwinder Path{/link} by night. Pridewing wyverns nest on the high cliffs.
• {b}The trolls of {link:malaka-jin}Malaka'jin{/link}.{/b} A {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} village sits at the southern foot of the mountains, where the road climbs up from the Barrens.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Age of the Druids.{/b} For ages uncounted, Stonetalon belonged to the forest and to those who guarded it. The druids of the peak and the children of {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link} kept the valleys green.
• {b}The Oracle.{/b} During the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} came to Stonetalon in search of the Oracle, and there the prophet {link:medivh}Medivh{/link} urged {link:orcs}orc{/link} and human to unite against the coming of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}.
• {b}The Coming of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.{/b} After the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, the Horde and the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} made their homes in {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. {link:sun-rock-retreat}Sun Rock Retreat{/link} was raised in the mountains, and the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} settled at {link:malaka-jin}Malaka'jin{/link}. No chronicle records the year of either.
• {b}The Goblin Invasion.{/b} The {link:venture-company}Venture Company{/link} came to the mountains to cut timber and dig ore. It stripped {link:windshear-crag}Windshear Crag{/link}, burned the {link:the-charred-vale}Charred Vale{/link} and poisoned the spirits of the land.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} Druids, shaman, {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} and gnomes now fight to heal what the goblins have broken. The goblins fight back, and the harpies, {link:grimtotem-clan}the Grimtotem{/link} and the fire spirits fight everyone.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Mountains",
			text = [=[• The shaman say that the spirits of Stonetalon are nearly blind with pain and rage. Those who listen for such things have heard the land itself cry out.
• The Bloodfury harpies are said to be the source of the {link:harpies}harpy{/link} plague across {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. The Witchwing of the {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link} came from these mountains.
• High on the peak, one of the eldest sons of {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link} once dwelt. His name was {link:keeper-ordanus}Ordanus{/link}, and he was taken away in secret when an enemy came hunting him.
• The Gaea seeds of {link:mirkfallon-lake}Mirkfallon Lake{/link} are said to resist corruption. The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} plant them in the ashes of the {link:the-charred-vale}Charred Vale{/link}, in the hope that a new forest will rise there one day.
• Beneath {link:boulderslide-ravine}Boulderslide Ravine{/link}, kobolds found a crystal called Resonite. Where it lay, something older than the kobolds was sleeping.]=],
		},
	},
})

